Purpose of JSON in APIs
What is the main purpose of JSON in APIs?

ANSWER = To send structured data between client and server..
JSON is a lightweight format used to organize and exchange data between a client (like a web app) and a server.
It allows APIs to send and receive data in a structured, easy-to-read way, making communication between different systems simple.

